when he looked at my work.

234
00:16:50,552 --> 00:16:53,528
Do you want to know what
the Duke said? It shows promise.

235
00:16:53,612 --> 00:16:57,128
Increase the accuracy.
You lose an now

236
00:16:57,212 --> 00:16:58,898
even you can't
deny that the Thousand

237
00:16:58,982 --> 00:17:03,038
Crests is as good as mine. That's
not true. Did you know I'm

238
00:17:03,122 --> 00:17:04,628
the first person
they allowed to stay

239
00:17:04,712 --> 00:17:06,608
in the castle after
presenting their work?

240
00:17:06,692 --> 00:17:08,978
I dare say it's quite the honor,
don't you?

241
00:17:09,122 --> 00:17:13,808
No one else can stay here. That's
what Dale told me. I refuse

242
00:17:13,892 --> 00:17:15,380
to let you save your breath.

243
00:17:15,620 --> 00:17:18,578
They gave me the honor
of moving into that tower.

244
00:17:18,662 --> 00:17:23,228
Only the chosen artisan stays there and
you've got nowhere to sleep.

245
00:17:23,312 --> 00:17:25,958
So try your best to make it
as a wandering merchant.

246
00:17:26,072 --> 00:17:28,778
What was he trying to achieve
by coming here?

247
00:17:28,862 --> 00:17:31,328
Is this some tactic
to crush my spirit?

248
00:17:31,442 --> 00:17:35,060
He just wanted an opportunity
to brag. Really?

249
00:17:35,750 --> 00:17:38,138
He can't gloat to his
friends now that they've left.

250
00:17:38,222 --> 00:17:41,940
So he came to you? How absurd.

251
00:17:45,070 --> 00:17:50,890
It's finished? Probably. What do
you think? Shall be honest.

252
00:17:53,080 --> 00:17:57,230
It looks well made. Listen.

253
00:18:19,300 --> 00:18:23,620
You did well. Scarecrow.

254
00:18:41,170 --> 00:18:43,900
Not quite.
He's not happy with it.

255
00:18:46,220 --> 00:18:49,130
But it's got
the right feel to it.

256
00:18:50,520 --> 00:18:52,770
In that sense,
it's better than his was.

257
00:18:52,950 --> 00:18:56,760
Make it more accurate than
it might be satisfying.

258
00:18:57,720 --> 00:19:02,250
Move her to this tower immediately.
We have two artisans now.

259
00:19:02,430 --> 00:19:08,560
There's no need to enlist
any more. Huh? Huh? Come.

260
00:19:12,480 --> 00:19:15,408
So I'm sorry to ask,
but does this mean the Duke was

261
00:19:15,492 --> 00:19:18,180
pleased with my sugar
confection? It wasn't clear.

262
00:19:18,630 --> 00:19:21,018
Let's just say he
didn't quite hate it.

263
00:19:21,132 --> 00:19:24,240
So you and Jonas Anders,
I believe

264
00:19:24,780 --> 00:19:26,058
the two of you will be tasked

265
00:19:26,142 --> 00:19:28,110
